WEBVTT

00:00:00.307 --> 00:00:02.472
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> I’d say my parents were pretty strict.

00:00:02.497 --> 00:00:09.976
I mean, they were…they were very strict about some things in particular; not so much about,

00:00:10.004 --> 00:00:12.873
I don’t know, playing outside, or things like that.

00:00:12.898 --> 00:00:15.885
In fact, I remember we used to go off and play all day

00:00:15.910 --> 00:00:19.406
and they wouldn’t know where we were or care what time we came back,

00:00:19.720 --> 00:00:22.378
so long as we didn’t miss a meal or something like that.

00:00:23.303 --> 00:00:25.237
But they were very strict about studying.

00:00:25.773 --> 00:00:32.560
They were very demanding: they wanted us to always be top of the class;

00:00:32.585 --> 00:00:34.776
they’d be very upset if we didn’t do well.

00:00:36.369 --> 00:00:39.928
On the other hand, they didn’t use to control how much homework we were doing,

00:00:39.953 --> 00:00:44.930
they never helped us with our homework, they just assumed we would be getting on with it,

00:00:45.706 --> 00:00:49.361
and they were very angry if we didn’t get – well, when I say ‘they’,

00:00:49.386 --> 00:00:55.581
my father much more than my mother – would be very angry if we didn’t do well in exams.

00:00:55.593 --> 00:00:58.839
My mother would be disappointed, but my father would be angry,

00:00:59.302 --> 00:01:05.039
and I remember with my A levels I got two As and a B, and he didn’t say

00:01:05.058 --> 00:01:13.143
‘Well done’, he just said, ‘Why did you get that B?’ And, er…so, my dad was controlling.

00:01:13.168 --> 00:01:17.480
I mean, he was pretty authoritarian and he controlled our tastes

00:01:17.505 --> 00:01:19.691
– well, he tried to control our tastes

00:01:19.927 --> 00:01:26.449
– in all sorts of things, in the sense that he thought we should agree with everything he liked.

00:01:26.720 --> 00:01:32.854
So, he didn’t approve of football, but he liked tennis, so watching tennis was fine,

00:01:32.879 --> 00:01:34.492
but watching football wasn’t.

00:01:35.093 --> 00:01:41.498
And he adored classical music, but loathed pop music, and I remember that, er,

00:01:41.511 --> 00:01:47.191
if he came in and my sister and I were watching a programme like <i>Top of the Pops</i> on television,

00:01:47.216 --> 00:01:52.040
he would immediately switch it off, and I think he actually broke some records

00:01:52.065 --> 00:01:55.281
that we’d bought of Beatles songs or something like that.